# Tokenwise

Use this rule when context may be expensive.

- Classify task before exploring.
- Use indexed/codegraph lookup for structural questions.
- Use text search for exact strings.
- Prefer narrow reads over whole-file reads.
- Stop exploring once the next edit or answer is known.
- Do not delegate broad exploration when the index can answer directly.
- Verify with the cheapest sufficient check.

